<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml v="1" site="mesh-lab.custom" epoch="1">
  <head>
    <title>Mesh lab</title>
    <meta name="headline" content="Two handhelds meet, derive fresh keys, and forget each other when the link dies."/>
    <meta name="tags" content="mesh, pfs, device, privacy"/>
  </head>
  <body>
    <page>
      <h1>Mesh lab</h1>
      <badge>field notes · link layer · no persistent session</badge>
      <p>A mesh link starts with an ephemeral P-256 agreement. The offer and accept are signed
      with the stable device key, so both sides know who they are talking to without making the
      conversation recoverable later.</p>
      <quote>Temporalness is the feature: the link, its keys, and its counters die together.</quote>
      <p>The two directional AES-256-GCM keys are derived once and never written down. A replayed
      frame fails its counter check and the link closes.</p>
    </page>
  </body>
</kml>
